# Boring-side monomorphization (V1): a free generic function called via
# explicit turbofish with fully-concrete type arguments at two different
# instantiations (int, string). Each site gets its own specialized,
# non-generic clone (`identity_int`, `identity_string`); the plain, still-
# generic `identity<T>` keeps compiling too (unused here, but must still be
# emitted as valid Rust — no other, non-turbofish call site touches it in
# this file).
def T identity(T x):
    x

print identity<int>(42)
print identity<string>("hi")
